# Coding & quality gates

## Deduplication (required)

- **Tests:** no copy-pasted HTTP/setup. Prefer `tests/conftest.py` helpers (`role_headers`, `assert_has_error_code`, …) or `@pytest.mark.parametrize`. Add a helper when the same sequence appears twice.
- **App:** extract shared utils when the same logic appears in 2+ places (e.g. helpers in `app/users/service.py`; `raise_validation` / `raise_field` in `app/shared/errors.py`). Do not invent layers for single use.

## Domain services (required)

- One `service.py` per domain package (`users`, `audit`, `outbox`, …) for use-case / write helpers. Same shape across domains — do not invent domain-specific layouts.
- Do **not** split use-cases into a `services/` package (`create.py`, `lifecycle.py`, `orgs.py`, …) or add `writer.py` / other one-off layers for thin writers.
- Shared query/validation helpers may live in a sibling `helpers.py` (not a use-case split). Models stay Declarative (schema only). Routers/workers import from that domain’s `service.py`.

## Call style (enforced by `scripts/check_call_style.py`)

- No `IfExp` / `BoolOp` / `Lambda` inside function-call arguments (`app/` + `tests/`).
- No nested non-constructor Calls inside call arguments (`app/` only; `models.py` / `schemas.py` exempt). CapWords constructors OK.
- Fix by extracting locals before the call.

## Lint / gates / CI

- **ruff** format + check on `app` `tests` `scripts` (see `pyproject.toml`).
- **FastAPI compile** via `scripts/check_fastapi_compile.py` (import `app.main:app`, OpenAPI path sanity).
- **Postman fresh** via `scripts/check_postman_collection.py` (committed `postman/User_Management_API*.json` match a fresh generate).
- **pytest** with **100%** line+branch coverage (`fail_under = 100`).
- Run `./scripts/gates.sh` before claiming done. Pre-commit uses `GATES_SKIP_TESTS=1`; full suite still in CI / `./init.sh`.
- Every gate/CI step must emit a **visible summary** (stdout `### …` and `$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` when set). New pipeline steps must follow `run_step` / the CI `| tee` + summary pattern.

## Tests = user flow

Drive behavior through real HTTP; mock only DB/external boundaries — never routers/services/schemas/RBAC.
